  "findings": [
    "All eleven old fixed-register admission reads are denied by stock SCM and silently return success/value zero. They did not establish missing TZ initialization.",
    "The v2 table differs from the common/no-TZ v1 layout. SEQ55/56 contain protected fixed values 0x2c5ffd/0x2f5ffd; SCM silently drops writes to them.",
    "The TZ caller discards the initializer return value. Eight compatible boot values cannot prove later protected initialization completed.",
    "XBL ClockDxe configures CPU PLL/mux state; CPU Agera lock status differs from GCC Fabia. No unproven CPU PLL direct access was added."
  ],
  "implemented": [
    "Exact unconditional SCM OSM subset enforced by engine and transport: SEQ15/31/32/57/58/72/76/88 in both clusters.",
    "Read-only admission checks the eight verified v2 boot values per cluster; old unreadable markers are removed.",
    "SEQ55/56 remain unchanged. Only the upper MEM-ACC threshold pair is written, including zero threshold predecessor0xff and corners1/2.",
    "Version2 80-byte handoff records profile1 and both0xff check masks; commit-last publication and rejection of old/incomplete contracts.",
    "Diagnostic names and build metadata distinguish table compatibility from protected post-init completion.",
    "Reproducible ELF audit verifies handlers, version-selected descriptors, source hashes, constants and production header drift."
  ],
  "validation": {
    "full_osm_suite": "passed: generator check, six driver test targets, 3072 vendor differential cases and64 integrated synthetic bin/revision/silicon combinations",
    "asan_ubsan": "passed: complete OSM suite and final changed CPRh/OSM/handoff contracts",
    "tz_audit_tests": 16,
    "handoff_python_tests": 4,
    "boot_bridge_python_tests": 49,
    "perfcontrol_integration_tests": 4,
    "QcomOSM_version": "1.4.0",
